From f6089e50b5f84a9a97e046121d289a458e07666a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mate Soos <soos.mate@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 23:11:38 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Gauss-elimination in-processing never reading the first
 row

Bug: find_implications_by_GE_core() brings the watched linerals into
reduced row echelon form and then scans the rows for implied units and
conflicts with "for(r = rank-1; r>0; --r)", so row 0 is never read.
Whatever the first row implies is lost: a unit x = c there is not
propagated, and if the only non-zero row is the conflict row 1 = 0
(rank 1), the conflict is missed.

Fix: include row 0 (rci_t is signed, so r>=0 terminates).

Effect: with -il 1 on a 799-variable 2-XNF fuzzer instance, GE
in-processing now finds 132471 implications instead of 56640, with the
same answer (UNSAT). A regression run of 200 2-XNF fuzzer instances
(xnf_fuzzer.py) shows no disagreement with CryptoMiniSat.

Found by reading the code while chasing an assertion failure in the -il
(GE in-processing) path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/solver.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/solver.cpp b/src/solver.cpp
index 240a959..cc836b0 100644
--- a/src/solver.cpp
+++ b/src/solver.cpp
@@ -1873,7 +1873,7 @@ bool solver::find_implications_by_GE_core(stats& s) {
   //read results
   list<lineral> linerals_;
   vec<var_t> idxs;
-  for(rci_t r = rank-1; r>0; --r) {
+  for(rci_t r = rank-1; r>=0; --r) {
     idxs.clear();
     for(rci_t c=0; (unsigned)c<n_vars; ++c) {
         if( mzd_read_bit(M, r, c) ) {
-- 
